§ 22.1037 Application requirements for offshore stations.

Applications for new [Offshore Radiotelephone Service](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=0943970f82f3badb3a1b2d56cd293d84&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:47:Chapter:I:Subchapter:B:Part:22:Subpart:I:22.1037)[stations](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=2ff08ee3dbd8ecf78e7f2c3e6adec40a&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:47:Chapter:I:Subchapter:B:Part:22:Subpart:I:22.1037) must contain an exhibit showing that:

(a) The applicant has notified all licensees of offshore stations located within 321.8 kilometers (200 miles) of the proposed offshore station, by providing the following data, at least 30 days before filing the application:

(1) The name, business address, [channel](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=2f3f2c2ee954828753562b46ef51ac1c&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:47:Chapter:I:Subchapter:B:Part:22:Subpart:I:22.1037) coordinator, and telephone number of the applicant;

(2) The location and geographical coordinates of the proposed station;

(3) The channel and type of [emission](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=123fb5751b93368d647724a5ba931ca9&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:47:Chapter:I:Subchapter:B:Part:22:Subpart:I:22.1037);

(4) The height and type of [antenna](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=e7ded8e1237471f618fe2e0e306fe916&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:47:Chapter:I:Subchapter:B:Part:22:Subpart:I:22.1037);

(5) The bearing of the main lobe of the antenna; and,

